    {
      "id": "9883652f9657e8bd8f32a8e0a16e2f1a2434969e",
      "short_id": "9883652f",
      "created_at": "2025-05-01T20:09:59.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "e38b1726bde59a74e1b92c7479eb4cb9456971ab"
      ],
      "title": "ftypes: Use C23 compatible checked arithmetic",
      "message": "ftypes: Use C23 compatible checked arithmetic\n\nAdd a header-only library for C23 checked integer arithmetic from\nhttps://github.com/jart/jtckdint\n\nUse it in the ftypes handling instead of the implementations in\nsafe-math. Note that the return value is opposite (true means\noverflow occurred).\n\nC23 stdckdint.h (and jtckdint.h) do not include implementations\nfor div, mod, and unary negation, where division by zero and,\nfor signed integers, cases like INT_MIN / -1 which overflow from\nINT_MAX + 1 for 2's complement. Those cases have to be handled\nseparately. Note that the divide by zero case, unlike the others,\ncan't really have a \"this is what the answer is if you just want\nthe result to wrap around,\" though that doesn't matter for the\nftypes/dfilter.\n\nPing #20144\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-04-29T23:08:15.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-05-01T20:09:59.000-04:00",
